Negative control for the forced states living IN the scenario menu (`R7-11`).

Takes the forced-state group out of the dropdown and leaves everything else —
the scenarios group still lists every track, the menu still opens, the presets
are still armable from a `force=` url — so the only claim that can go red is the
ruled one: the ONE menu is where a page's non-live state is chosen, scenarios in
one group and forced states in another. Without it the presets are back to being
a control of their own beside Debug│Code│Scenario, which is the placement the
ruling removed.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the scenario-menu forced-group case — the menu offers every url preset as
its own labelled group beside the scenarios.

